stripeco-support: Hi team, after upgrading our client we started getting 400s from POST /v1/rerank. Error body: {"error":"invalid_request","message":"candidates must be an array","status":400}. Repro attached.

stripeco-support: curl -s -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/rerank \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-cust-xxx" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "queries":[{"id":"q-1","text":"how to cancel subscription"}],
    "candidates": {
      "c1":{"id":"c1","text":"Cancel in dashboard"},
      "c2":{"id":"c2","text":"Open support ticket"}
    },
    "topk": "2"
  }'

nina (support): thanks for the repro. Can you paste the raw response headers and confirm client lib version?

stripeco-support: headers show Content-Type: application/json; client version is stripeco-sdk-js 4.0.0 (we rolled it out today).

omar (eng-runtime): looks like the body is sending candidates as an object (map) instead of an array. Also topk is a string. Both can trigger schema validation. Can you try sending candidates as an array and topk as a number?

stripeco-support: tried manual curl with candidates as array and numeric topk -> works. The bug is reproducible with our app build only. We dug in and found the batching change in 4.0.0 where we de-duplicated candidates by id and kept them in an object map for the batch payload. The SDK JSON.stringify step forgot to convert back to array for single-request mode.

casey (sdk): thanks for the detective work. We shipped a batching refactor that kept candidates keyed by id during dedupe. In some code paths we were calling JSON.stringify on the map directly. Repro in node: const m = {c1:{id:'c1',text:'a'}}; JSON.stringify({queries, candidates:m, topk:'2'}) -> server sees candidates as object.

casey (sdk): short term: patch incoming to coerce maps to arrays before send and validate topk type. Proposed fix snippet:
```
function serializeCandidates(c){
  if (Array.isArray(c)) return c;
  if (c && typeof c === 'object') return Object.values(c);
  return [];
}
```
We will cut 4.0.1 in next 12 hours.

omar (eng-runtime): INF-4972 created: "rerank: surface 'received object, expected array' in error message and log candidate-type mismatch in telemetry". Gateway logs show AJV error pathting but our error message collapsed to generic string. We'll include AJV error detail for this endpoint only.

stripeco-support: appreciated. One more oddity: we sometimes saw the body double-encoded (strings containing JSON). Could that be from our proxy?

infra-bot: Log export attached to INF-4972 includes raw request bodies. A handful look double-encoded, but majority are map->object. Content-Type for failing requests is application/json.

nina (support): action items: 1) casey to release SDK 4.0.1 with normalization and a non-breaking warning log; 2) omar to update error payload to include AJV hint text for type mismatches; 3) support to notify affected customers and advise workaround (Object.values(candidates) + Number(topk)).

casey (sdk): publishing patch now, will post release notes to #support and tag customers.

stripeco-support: thanks — holding rollout until 4.0.1. Please cc us on release notes and INF-4972.

nina (support): noted and done. Closing this thread for now, will reopen if stripeco sees anything after SDK update. :thumbsup:
